---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/Colophon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { getPublishedPosts } from '../lib/writing';

const showWriting = (await getPublishedPosts()).length > 0;
const access = site.links.edgarMiner ?? `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Edgar Miner access')}`;
const accessText = site.links.edgarMiner ? 'try it' : 'ask for access';
---
<Base title={site.name} description={site.description}>
  <Nav slot="nav" showWriting={showWriting} />
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>{site.headline}</h1>

    <p class="purpose">I'm Chandni, an engineer who keeps starting companies. At ThinkMocha, I'm turning SEC filings into structured data and knowledge graphs for investment research. <a href="/work/edgar-miner/">Edgar Miner</a> connects the dots between companies: who supplies whom, who owns what, and where the dependencies are.</p>

    <p>If you work in investment research, email me to <a href={access}>{accessText}</a>.</p>

    {site.hero && <Media items={[site.hero]} />}

    <h2>How ThinkMocha started</h2>

    <p>ThinkMocha started somewhere very different. One evening, I couldn't convince my then three-year-old to eat her vegetables, so I made her an AI storybook where she was the heroine of a veggie world. She ate the vegetables; I started making books for friends and family, weaving their children's cultures and everyday lives into the stories.</p>

    <p>That became <a href="/work/talewriter/">Talewriter</a>. I built it myself and ran a pilot that put 50+ personalized books into a Manhattan preschool.</p>

    <h2>Earlier work</h2>

    <p>Before that, I spent six years building backend systems. At Rakuten, I led backend development for <a href="https://www.rakuten.com/dining">Rakuten Dining</a>, a rewards product with 10,000+ restaurants, and helped teams adopt serverless architecture, reducing infrastructure costs by 80%. At <a href="https://www.serverless.com/">Serverless</a>, I rebuilt billing on Stripe and cut processing time by 98%. Earlier, I shipped a Chrome extension that <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2016/08/23/slices-new-browser-add-on-will-email-you-when-prices-drop/">TechCrunch wrote about</a>.</p>

    <h2>Other projects</h2>

    <p><a href="/work/fundraising-agent/">Fundraising Agent</a> automates investor outreach for founders, bringing the work from 20 hours a week to under two. An events app never made it beyond my friends. I also won three hackathons for projects involving image recognition, event discovery, and an Arduino scoring system.</p>

    <p>I earned my Tech MBA at NYU Stern in 2026 and screened deep-tech startups for its accelerator. I also apply to YC every year.</p>

    <p class="lines">Some things have worked. Others haven't made it very far. I usually come away with another question I want to build something around. {site.links.ideas && <a href={site.links.ideas}>Here's the list.</a>}</p>

    <p>I speak five languages, too. Happy to start there.</p>

    <p class="ps">If you research companies through SEC filings, I'd love to hear what you're trying to figure out. Email me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <Colophon slot="colophon" />
</Base>
